codex
The required harness cannot reach any oracle: OpenRouter returns HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded (total limit)” on every retry. The harness correctly refuses to count those errors as model failures, so no hardness verdict can be manufactured from them. I’ll preserve that script-owned evidence, verify the two G9 arm transcripts have the same honest failure mode, and finish the handoff with the exact rerun needed once quota is available.
codex
One more schema audit caught a real representational issue: the answer was labeled a polynomial but serialized as a flat integer list. I’m correcting it to the natural \(32\times2\) finite-field coefficient matrix used by the displayed block bases. This preserves the same 64 field elements and search space, while making the certificate form honest and non-flattened. Because it changes the output contract, I’ll rerun all local gates and the script-owned harness attempts afterward.
apply patch
