codex
Implemented a Track B generator from the characteristic-\(p\) coefficient identity in Lemma 2.6 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1701.06906v1).

Files:

- [gen_1701_06906.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1701.06906/gen_1701_06906.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1701.06906/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1701.06906/README.md)
- [bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1701.06906/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1701.06906/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1701.06906/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates all pass:

- Guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference method: 12,825,889 operations on the configured shipping candidate.
- Answer: \(32\times2\) finite-field matrix, 106 estimated tokens worst-of-10,000 seeds.
- Compact route: 288 operations.
- G1 rerun after final changes: 12/12.

The result is parked, not rejected or submission-ready. The bare oracle run reached \(p\approx10^9\): two vendors failed, but the third slot exhausted four retries with OpenRouter HTTP 403. Thus `harden.py` correctly issued no verdict. Both G9 comparison arms were likewise blocked by quota. A funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to rerun:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1701_06906.py
```
